Review fix (T8, suspected lost update in apply_plan): confirmed by a failing test, fixed.

apply_plan(store, plan) applied a plan computed before it took the lock, and wrote the map and the answers in two
separate lock holds. A claim the Checker re-anchored between planning and applying (now current at HEAD) was
marked stale again and its verdict reset. Now apply_plan holds the lock once for both files, applies a claim's
result only if the claim still has the anchors the plan classified (and isn't retired), returns the ids it
skipped, and advances the map's commit only when no map claim was skipped. The CLI's `refresh apply` (T7.5) does
not use apply_plan (it plans inside the lock), so this fixes the library call only. Adds
tests/review/test_review_apply_plan.py (fails without the fix).

Apply from the repo root: git apply docs/patches/review-apply-plan-lost-update.patch

